# The real mod under `claude -p` (issue #246, Claude Code 2.1.312)

Made for the PR of issue #246. A throwaway step of the e2e harness (not committed) ran the scenario "A question and my answer are
listed by /track qa" up to the answer of the dialog, ended the interactive session with `/exit`, and then ran, in the same clone
and with the same config folder, `claude -p --continue "<prompt>"` with the real mod (`--plugin-dir plugins/artifact-tracking`)
against the fake Messages API. `claude -p` draws nothing (`$.session.surfaces()` is `[]`), so every reply is the whole text. The
call was read back from the transcript of the interactive session (the replay). The guard `cc-plugin-sec-default` was loaded and
was not bypassed. Grade: *verified-kit* (a headless run is never *verified-live*). The model was the fake. The lines
`its prompt.compose hook was skipped` on stderr come from the guard that runs first on this machine.

=== claude -p --continue "/track qa" (exit 0)
